{"kind":"report","text":"Approved exact head 6b995c5e227f7fa5ff235bfcc301fd7863361df2, all seven artifacts with packages/policy/README.md first. Independently read the complete five-file revision-2 delta; the README and policy.ts are byte-identical to the already reviewed first candidate. Both findings in b552e1d6 are answered for this explicitly limited change.\n\nArchitecture: the rule reads Room-owned proposal.changed, considers the added/modified path or rename destination, and ignores deleted paths and rename sources. A clean repair that removes imported jj conflict data is therefore no longer refused as unresolved. Introducing or modifying a root .jjconflict-base-* or .jjconflict-side-* path still produces the helpful jj-conflicts refusal. The exact diff is built by the Room before these rules run; this does not trust an author's reported changed paths. The shared act meter, bounded diff and subsequent hard claim checks remain required by the existing R-ADM-1 change.\n\nSecurity: policy only adds a refusal; it does not waive containment or other platform invariants, and configuration-recovery lanes still skip policy while retaining the admin/platform boundary. Added/modified conflict data and rename destinations are covered; nested names and ordinary names that merely contain jjconflict are accepted. The rule is honestly described as detecting introduced or changed conflict data, not as proving the whole head conflict-free. An unrelated edit above untouched conflict data remains accepted and has an explicit test. The Room-owned bounded root-entry fact and the live per-change history route remain open within the complete scope (amendment 3/open point 39); this approval neither removes nor completes them.\n\nSimplification: checking one structured changed-path list preserves ordinary repairs and avoids requiring an extra whole-tree scan or broad path-union interpretation inside the expression. The reason/fix, generated policy and documentation now describe the same observable behavior. The budget corpus reports the actual additional status test: at 500 paths propose uses 5,012 steps/172,286 inspected bytes, and at the measured largest 1,461-path input 14,622 steps/511,636 bytes. Both stay within the existing 25,000-step/four-MiB act budget; the input bound remains unchanged. These are deterministic evaluator measurements, not a deployed CPU timing guarantee.\n\nValidation at this exact detached head: npm ci; complete root strict typecheck; all 198 Policy Node tests and 197 Policy Workers tests passed with one existing Workers-only skip; the same corpus verifies additions, modifications, deleting all marker data, renaming into/out of markers, untouched-data limitation, recovery bypass, rule order, budgets and replay. Ran the documented root compile-policy command: generated policy.json remained byte-identical and git status was clean. No live deployment was performed. Merge must preserve the already landed amendment-3 text while adding this earlier amendment's limited-check clarification.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:b1fffcaca8fdeca11fd5dd158447f5c1d9065883","binding":"assigned","head":"6b995c5e227f7fa5ff235bfcc301fd7863361df2","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:317f18864194380f4dd4b225467f233fcdb96610\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:dead62c344a422161be9b5064cd15ac297028381\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:317f18864194380f4dd4b225467f233fcdb96610","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}